---
/**
 * Field note: "Avoid the trap of 'fake' A/B tests in business"
 * → /field-notes/fake-ab-test-trap/
 *
 * Deliberately not the site's visual system: light graph paper instead of the
 * site's dark canvas, Space Grotesk display instead of Fraunces, sans body
 * throughout. Reads on a phone, projects in a lit room.
 *
 * Terminology follows the Kit A/B Test Playbook: exposure event, conversion
 * event, baseline rate, MDE in percentage points.
 */
---

<div class="ab">
  <div class="ab-inner">
    <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
    <section class="ab-hero">
      <p class="ab-kicker">Field note &middot; causal inference</p>
      <h1>
        Avoid the trap of <span class="ab-fake">&ldquo;fake&rdquo;</span>
        A/B tests in business
      </h1>
      <p class="ab-dek">
        The randomized trial is the gold standard. Most business questions
        can&rsquo;t have one. Saying which is which is your job.
      </p>
      <p class="ab-scroll" aria-hidden="true">scroll &darr;</p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 01 ============ -->
    <section class="ab-card">
      <p class="ab-num">01</p>
      <h2>It&rsquo;s a trial, not a split.</h2>
      <p>
        I say <strong>RCT</strong>, randomized controlled trial, because the
        long name says what the short one hides. You randomize. You keep a
        control. You run a trial of one specific thing.
      </p>
      <p>
        The question it answers is narrow: did the exposure cause the
        conversion, or did chance?
      </p>

      <figure class="ab-fig">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 340 130" role="img" aria-labelledby="d1t">
          <title id="d1t"
            >An exposed group converting at 12 percent above an unexposed
            control group converting at 10 percent; the two-point gap is the
            causal effect.</title
          >
          <rect x="2" y="8" width="104" height="40" rx="4" class="s-box s-blue" />
          <text x="54" y="33" class="s-lbl">exposed</text>
          <path d="M112 28 H190" class="s-arrow s-blue-st" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
          <rect x="200" y="8" width="138" height="40" rx="4" class="s-box s-blue" />
          <text x="269" y="33" class="s-lbl">converts 12%</text>

          <rect x="2" y="82" width="104" height="40" rx="4" class="s-box s-ghost" />
          <text x="54" y="107" class="s-lbl s-dim">not exposed</text>
          <path d="M112 102 H190" class="s-arrow s-ghost-st" marker-end="url(#ahg)" />
          <rect x="200" y="82" width="138" height="40" rx="4" class="s-box s-ghost" />
          <text x="269" y="107" class="s-lbl s-dim">converts 10%</text>

          <path d="M269 48 V82" class="s-arrow s-amber-st s-dash" marker-end="url(#aha)" />

          <defs>
            <marker id="ah" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" refX="6" refY="3.5" orient="auto">
              <path d="M0 0 L7 3.5 L0 7 z" class="s-blue-fill" />
            </marker>
            <marker id="ahg" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" refX="6" refY="3.5" orient="auto">
              <path d="M0 0 L7 3.5 L0 7 z" class="s-ghost-fill" />
            </marker>
            <marker id="aha" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" refX="6" refY="3.5" orient="auto">
              <path d="M0 0 L7 3.5 L0 7 z" class="s-amber-fill" />
            </marker>
          </defs>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>
          <strong class="c-amber">Those 2 points are the causal effect.</strong>
          The control group stands in for a world that never happened.
          Randomizing is what licenses the substitution.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 02 ============ -->
    <section class="ab-card">
      <p class="ab-num">02</p>
      <h2>Everyone will want one. For everything.</h2>
      <p>
        Stakeholders don&rsquo;t push for tests because they love statistics.
        They push because the world is uncertain and a p-value looks like solid
        ground.
      </p>
      <p class="ab-quote">
        &ldquo;Can we just A/B test it?&rdquo;
        <span>— asked about a decision that cannot be A/B tested</span>
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 03 ============ -->
    <section class="ab-card">
      <p class="ab-num">03</p>
      <h2>Splitting traffic isn&rsquo;t testing.</h2>
      <p>
        Send half your users somewhere different and you have a split. You have
        a trial only if you fixed the rules <em>before</em> you saw the numbers.
      </p>

      <div class="ab-split">
        <div class="ab-col ab-col--bad">
          <p class="ab-col-h">Theater</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Split the traffic</li>
            <li>Watch the dashboard daily</li>
            <li>Pick the winning metric after looking</li>
            <li>Stop when it looks good</li>
            <li>Ship the story</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="ab-col ab-col--good">
          <p class="ab-col-h">A trial</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Randomize <em>users</em>, not page views</li>
            <li>Name one conversion event first</li>
            <li>Set the MDE before you look</li>
            <li>Stop at the sample size you planned</li>
            <li>Ship the decision you agreed to</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="ab-note">
        <strong>MDE</strong> is the minimum detectable effect: the smallest lift
        worth shipping, say +1.5 points on a 5% baseline. Choose it first. It
        sets your sample size, and it is what separates <em>real</em> from
        <em>worth it</em>: an effect can be statistically significant and still
        too small to justify the work.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 04 ============ -->
    <section class="ab-card">
      <p class="ab-num">04</p>
      <p class="ab-wall">Wall 1</p>
      <h2>There is no multiverse.</h2>
      <p>
        Steve Jobs did not A/B test the iPhone. Not because he was bold, but
        because you cannot launch into two universes and compare. One-shot,
        irreversible decisions have no control group.
      </p>

      <figure class="ab-fig">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 340 120" role="img" aria-labelledby="d2t">
          <title id="d2t"
            >A timeline reaching a launch point, from which one solid branch is
            the world that happened and three faded branches are worlds you can
            never observe.</title
          >
          <text x="2" y="12" class="s-cap s-dim-fill" text-anchor="start">worlds you can&rsquo;t see</text>
          <path d="M100 66 C 160 66, 190 40, 300 28" class="s-arrow s-ghost-st s-dash" />
          <path d="M100 66 C 160 66, 190 86, 300 100" class="s-arrow s-ghost-st s-dash" />
          <path d="M100 66 C 160 66, 190 98, 300 116" class="s-arrow s-ghost-st s-dash" />

          <path d="M2 66 H300" class="s-arrow s-blue-st s-thick" />
          <circle cx="100" cy="66" r="5.5" class="s-amber-fill" />
          <text x="100" y="88" class="s-cap s-amber-fill">launch</text>
          <text x="300" y="56" class="s-cap s-blue-fill" text-anchor="end">the world you got</text>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>After launch there is no control group left to compare against.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 05 ============ -->
    <section class="ab-card">
      <p class="ab-num">05</p>
      <p class="ab-wall">Wall 2</p>
      <h2>The arithmetic says no.</h2>
      <p>
        &ldquo;Just measure revenue.&rdquo; Usually you can&rsquo;t. Sample size
        is set by your baseline rate and your MDE, and a rare event punishes you
        on both.
      </p>
      <p>
        Take 2,000 visitors a week and a 2% purchase rate. Detecting a 10% lift
        (an MDE of 0.2 points) needs about
        <strong>78,400 users per group</strong>.
      </p>

      <figure class="ab-fig ab-chart">
        <p class="ab-chart-h">Users needed per group, for a 10% lift</p>

        <div class="ab-bar">
          <p class="ab-bar-metric">
            Bought something <span class="ab-bar-n">78,400</span>
          </p>
          <div class="ab-bar-fill ab-bar-fill--red" style="width:100%"></div>
          <p class="ab-bar-sub">2% baseline &middot; MDE 0.2pp &middot; about 18 months</p>
        </div>

        <div class="ab-bar">
          <p class="ab-bar-metric">
            Reached checkout <span class="ab-bar-n c-blue">6,400</span>
          </p>
          <div class="ab-bar-fill ab-bar-fill--blue" style="width:8.2%"></div>
          <p class="ab-bar-sub">20% baseline &middot; MDE 2pp &middot; about 6 weeks</p>
        </div>

        <figcaption>n &asymp; 16 &times; p(1&minus;p) / MDE&sup2;, at 95% significance and 80% power</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p class="ab-note">
        Eighteen months. The feature gets rewritten twice, and whoever asked for
        the test has changed teams.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 06 ============ -->
    <section class="ab-card ab-card--turn">
      <p class="ab-num">06</p>
      <h2>Test one link, not the whole chain.</h2>
      <p>
        So narrow the question. Make the conversion event an earlier step in the
        journey, one with the traffic to support a real test. That is the second
        bar: six weeks instead of eighteen months.
      </p>

      <figure class="ab-fig">
        <p class="ab-chart-h">A user journey</p>
        <ol class="ab-chain">
          <li>Lands on the page</li>
          <li class="is-tested">Sees the new offer</li>
          <li class="is-tested is-goal">Reaches checkout</li>
          <li>Buys</li>
          <li>Comes back next month</li>
        </ol>
        <figcaption>
          <span class="c-blue">The trial settles the highlighted link.</span> The
          rest of the chain is not in the test and never was.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p>
        The scope is the point. The trial did not rule on the initiative. It
        settled one decision inside it. Everything downstream stays a judgment
        call, made by the people paid to make it.
      </p>
      <p class="ab-note">
        Say the scope out loud, every time. Left unsaid, a win on checkout rate
        gets retold as proof the initiative makes money, and it will be your
        name on the chart.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 07 ============ -->
    <section class="ab-card">
      <p class="ab-num">07</p>
      <h2>No trial possible? You still have tools.</h2>
      <p>
        None of these match an RCT. All of them beat a confident guess, and all
        of them come with error bars.
      </p>

      <ul class="ab-tools">
        <li>
          <span class="t-name">Staged rollout</span>
          <span class="t-desc">Ship to some regions first, hold the rest back. Cheapest thing here, and impossible to arrange after launch.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="t-name">Switchback test</span>
          <span class="t-desc">Can&rsquo;t split users? Split time. Flip the change on and off on a schedule.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="t-name">Difference-in-differences</span>
          <span class="t-desc">Compare the change in your group against the change in a similar untouched group.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="t-name">Regression discontinuity</span>
          <span class="t-desc">Some rule has a hard cutoff. Compare people just above it to people just below.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="t-name">Synthetic control</span>
          <span class="t-desc">Build a weighted twin of the treated market out of the untreated ones.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="t-name">Pre/post analysis</span>
          <span class="t-desc">A clean before and after, and the honesty to list everything else that changed that week.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="ab-note">
        Most of these cost nothing, <em>if</em> you are in the room before the
        launch. Afterwards they are gone. Being early beats being clever.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ CLOSER ============ -->
    <section class="ab-close">
      <p class="ab-num">The job</p>
      <p class="ab-shout">Be a force for the right tool in each circumstance.</p>
      <p>
        Don&rsquo;t cave under pressure to rubber-stamp a preconceived narrative
        with your expertise. Someone always has an agenda and a slide already
        written. Your signature on a fake test is the only thing that makes it
        dangerous.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ FOOTER ============ -->
    <footer class="ab-foot">
      <p class="ab-foot-h">Read these</p>
      <p>
        Kohavi, Tang &amp; Xu, <em>Trustworthy Online Controlled Experiments</em>
        (2020), the chapter on what to do when you can&rsquo;t run a test.
      </p>
      <p>
        Huntington-Klein, <em>The Effect</em> (2022), free at
        <a href="https://theeffectbook.net" rel="noopener">theeffectbook.net</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="ab-back">
        <a href="/field-notes/">← All field notes</a>
        <a href="/">aleberriz.com</a>
      </p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@500;700&display=swap');

  /* Light "lab notebook" palette. Scoped, so none of this reaches another
     note. `.ab` paints the full-bleed page; `.ab-inner` is the text column. */
  .ab {
    --paper: #faf8f3;
    --ink: #14181f;
    --body: #3c444f;
    --dim: #5b6472;
    --blue: #1257c9;
    --red: #c42b1c;
    --amber: #a1600a;
    --rule: rgba(20, 24, 31, 0.14);
    --grid: rgba(18, 87, 201, 0.07);

    min-height: 100vh;
    color: var(--body);
    font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    background-color: var(--paper);
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(to right, var(--grid) 1px, transparent 1px),
      linear-gradient(to bottom, var(--grid) 1px, transparent 1px);
    background-size: 26px 26px;
  }

  .ab-inner {
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.25rem 4rem;
  }

  .ab p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .ab strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .ab em { font-style: italic; }
  .ab a { color: var(--blue); }

  .ab-kicker,
  .ab-num,
  .ab-wall,
  .ab-scroll,
  .ab-col-h,
  .ab-foot-h,
  .ab-chart-h {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--dim);
  }

  /* ---- hero ---- */
  .ab-hero { padding: 4rem 0 3.5rem; }
  .ab-hero h1 {
    margin: 1.25rem 0 1.5rem;
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 9.2vw, 3.4rem);
    line-height: 1.04;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-wrap: balance;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .ab-fake {
    color: var(--red);
    text-decoration: line-through;
    text-decoration-thickness: 4px;
  }
  .ab-dek {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink);
    max-width: 32ch;
  }
  .ab-scroll { margin-top: 2.5rem; }

  /* ---- cards ---- */
  .ab-card,
  .ab-close {
    padding: 3rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .ab-card h2 {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1.25rem;
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 7vw, 2.15rem);
    line-height: 1.12;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .ab-wall { color: var(--red); display: block; margin-top: 0.4rem; }
  .ab-card--turn h2 { color: var(--blue); }

  .ab-note {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--amber);
    font-size: 0.97rem;
  }

  .ab-quote {
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0;
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.45rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--amber);
  }
  .ab-quote span {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--dim);
  }

  /* ---- figures ---- */
  .ab-fig { margin: 1.75rem 0; }
  .ab-fig svg { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
  .ab-fig figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  .c-amber { color: var(--amber); }
  .c-blue { color: var(--blue); }

  .s-box { fill: none; stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .s-blue { stroke: var(--blue); fill: rgba(18, 87, 201, 0.07); }
  .s-ghost { stroke: var(--dim); fill: none; stroke-dasharray: 4 4; }
  .s-arrow { fill: none; stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .s-blue-st { stroke: var(--blue); }
  .s-ghost-st { stroke: var(--dim); }
  .s-amber-st { stroke: var(--amber); }
  .s-dash { stroke-dasharray: 4 5; opacity: 0.7; }
  .s-thick { stroke-width: 2.5; }
  .s-blue-fill { fill: var(--blue); }
  .s-amber-fill { fill: var(--amber); }
  .s-ghost-fill { fill: var(--dim); }
  .s-dim-fill { fill: var(--dim); }
  .s-lbl {
    fill: var(--ink);
    font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .s-dim { fill: var(--dim); }
  .s-cap {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
  }
  /* CSS beats the SVG presentation attribute, so mirror it explicitly. */
  .ab text.s-lbl { text-anchor: middle; }
  .ab text.s-cap { text-anchor: middle; }
  .ab text.s-cap[text-anchor='start'] { text-anchor: start; }
  .ab text.s-cap[text-anchor='end'] { text-anchor: end; }

  /* ---- theater vs trial ---- */
  .ab-split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }
  .ab-col {
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
  }
  .ab-col--bad { border-top: 3px solid var(--red); }
  .ab-col--good { border-top: 3px solid var(--blue); }
  .ab-col--bad .ab-col-h { color: var(--red); }
  .ab-col--good .ab-col-h { color: var(--blue); }
  .ab-col ul { margin: 0.75rem 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .ab-col li {
    padding: 0.4rem 0 0.4rem 1.3rem;
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    position: relative;
  }
  .ab-col--bad li::before { content: '×'; color: var(--red); position: absolute; left: 0; font-weight: 700; }
  .ab-col--good li::before { content: '✓'; color: var(--blue); position: absolute; left: 0; font-weight: 700; }

  /* ---- bar chart (HTML, so labels wrap on narrow screens) ---- */
  .ab-chart-h { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .ab-bar { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .ab-bar-metric {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .ab-bar-fill { height: 1.6rem; min-width: 0.4rem; }
  .ab-bar-fill--red { background: var(--red); }
  .ab-bar-fill--blue { background: var(--blue); }
  .ab-bar-n {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    white-space: nowrap;
    float: right;
  }
  .ab-bar-sub { margin: 0.45rem 0 0; font-size: 0.87rem; color: var(--dim); }

  /* ---- journey chain ---- */
  .ab-chain { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .ab-chain li {
    position: relative;
    margin-left: 0.55rem;
    padding: 0.55rem 0 0.55rem 1.4rem;
    border-left: 2px dashed var(--rule);
    color: var(--dim);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .ab-chain li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: -5px;
    top: 1.05rem;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #c3c8d0;
  }
  .ab-chain li:first-child { padding-top: 0; }
  .ab-chain li:first-child::before { top: 0.5rem; }
  .ab-chain li:last-child { border-left-color: transparent; padding-bottom: 0; }
  .ab-chain .is-tested {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--blue);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .ab-chain .is-tested::before { background: var(--blue); }
  .ab-chain .is-goal::after {
    content: 'conversion event';
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.2rem;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--blue);
  }

  /* ---- toolbox ---- */
  .ab-tools { margin: 1.5rem 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .ab-tools li { padding: 0.85rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .t-name {
    display: block;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--blue);
  }
  .t-desc { display: block; margin-top: 0.3rem; font-size: 0.97rem; line-height: 1.5; }

  /* ---- closer ---- */
  .ab-close { border-top: 3px solid var(--ink); }
  .ab-close .ab-num { color: var(--ink); }
  .ab-shout {
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.85rem, 8vw, 2.6rem);
    line-height: 1.06;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  /* ---- footer ---- */
  .ab-foot {
    padding: 2.5rem 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  .ab-back { margin-top: 1.75rem; display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; }

  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .ab-split { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }

  /* ---- present mode (?present), for projection ---- */
  :global(html.present) .ab { font-size: 1.3rem; }
  :global(html.present) .ab-inner { max-width: 52rem; }
  :global(html.present) .ab-foot { display: none; }
</style>
